---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import Row from '../../components/Row.astro';
import { RELEASE, TRIAL } from '../../data/site';

// Install and first launch, in the app's own words (the setup screens in
// crates/vault-tauri/dist/app.js; the /docs/ hub's Getting started keeps a
// short version that links here).
const win = RELEASE.windows;
const OUTLINE = [
  { id: 'before', title: 'Before you start' },
  { id: 'install', title: 'Install' },
  { id: 'set-up', title: 'Set up' },
  { id: 'next', title: 'What to do next' },
];
---
<Guide
  path="/docs/getting-started/"
  lede={`Download the Zaaheen installer for Windows, open it, then choose Begin set up. Setting up takes about three minutes: you create your account (your ${TRIAL.days}-day free trial starts straight away, no card needed), choose where your memories live, and connect your first AI app.`}
  outline={OUTLINE}
>
  <section class="docs-section">
    <Row id="before" title="Before you start" where="Windows">
      {!RELEASE.available && <p><strong>Zaaheen for Windows is coming soon.</strong> These steps are
         how it works once you can download it.</p>}
      <p>Zaaheen {RELEASE.version} is a {RELEASE.stage.toLowerCase()} for {win.arch} Windows and has
         been tested on {win.tested}. It is not available for macOS or Linux yet.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="install" title="Install" where="Windows installer">
      <p>Open the installer you downloaded. Two things happen while it installs:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Windows says the publisher is unknown.</strong> Zaaheen is in beta, and the
            installer is not code-signed yet; signing comes before the full launch. Choose
            <em>More info</em>, then <em>Run anyway</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Windows asks for administrator permission.</strong> Zaaheen installs for everyone
            on the computer, so Windows asks once. It does not need administrator rights to run
            afterwards.</li>
      </ul>
    </Row>

    <Row id="set-up" title="Set up" where="Begin set up">
      <p>Open Zaaheen and choose <em>Begin set up</em>. It walks you through five steps:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Your account.</strong> Choose <em>Create an account</em> or <em>Sign in</em>. This
            opens your web browser. Your {TRIAL.days}-day free trial starts when you create your
            account, and no card is needed. Signing in never shares your memories with us.</li>
        <li><strong>Where to keep your memories.</strong> The usual place suits most people. You can
            change it later from Settings with <em>Move my memories…</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Your first AI app.</strong> Pick the app you use and follow the steps, or choose
            <em>I'll connect one later</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Your first memory.</strong> Tell Zaaheen something your AI apps should know about
            you, then choose <em>Keep this memory</em>, or <em>Skip for now</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Tidying up.</strong> Choose whether Zaaheen keeps your memory tidy on its own,
            then <em>Finish setup</em>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>The first time, Zaaheen also downloads what it needs to search your memories. It does this
         in the background, and you can use Zaaheen while it finishes.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="next" title="What to do next" where="Agents">
      <p>Connect the AI apps you use, each once, from the <em>Agents</em> tab:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/docs/connect-claude/">Connect Claude</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/connect-cursor/">Connect Cursor</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/connect-chatgpt/">Connect ChatGPT</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/connect-other-apps/">Connect other AI apps</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>If something doesn't work as described, see <a href="/docs/troubleshooting/">Fixing common
         problems</a>.</p>
    </Row>
  </section>
</Guide>
